<article>
  <div class="post-meta"><span>2025</span><span class="blog-tag">Taxes 2026</span><span>Guzman Tax Accounting</span></div>
  <div class="post-featured-img"><img src="/assets/taxes-banner.webp" alt="Tax Preparation 2026 for the Latino Community" loading="lazy"/></div>
  <div class="post-content"><p>Tax season has already started, and thousands of Latino families are asking the same questions: When do I need to file? How much will I get back? What documents do I need?</p><h2>When Is the Filing Deadline for 2026?</h2><p>The general deadline to file your federal taxes is <strong>April 15, 2026</strong>. If you need more time, you can request an extension until October 15, 2026.</p><h2>Documents You'll Need</h2><ul><li>Form W-2 (from your employer)</li><li>Form 1099 (if you are an independent contractor)</li><li>Social Security Number (SSN) or ITIN</li><li>Dependent information (children, family members)</li><li>Prior-year tax return (if applicable)</li></ul><h2>Why Use a Professional?</h2><p>At Guzman Tax & Accounting, we help Latino individuals and businesses file correctly, avoid costly mistakes, and maximize their legal benefits. Spanish-speaking service available.</p><a href="/en/consultation" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:8px;">Schedule Your Consultation</a></div>
  <div style="margin-top:40px;padding:28px;background:var(--gray);border-radius:12px;text-align:center;">
    <h3 style="margin-bottom:10px;">Need Help with Your Taxes?</h3>
    <p style="color:var(--text-light);margin-bottom:20px;">Schedule a consultation with our experts. Bilingual service available.</p>
    <a href="/en/consultation" class="btn btn-primary">Consultation</a>
  </div>
</article>
